{"description": "Extracts text elements from every new or changed document in the RAG inventory through the rag_core extractor registry; corrupt documents are marked failed without failing the flow.", "displayName": "RAG - Extract Text.step", "flowMetadata": {"inputPorts": [{"name": "_rgex_inventory", "displayName": "_rgex_inventory", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "type": "table", "id": "_rgex_inventory", "label": "_rgex_inventory"}], "outputPorts": [{"name": "_rgex_invout", "displayName": "_rgex_invout", "minEntries": 1, "maxEntries": 1, "columnDelta": null, "type": "table"}]}, "metadataVersion": 1, "name": "RAG - Extract Text.step", "properties": {}, "templates": {"SAS": "/******************************************************************************\n * Copyright \u00a9 2026, SAS Institute Inc., Cary, NC, USA.  All Rights Reserved.\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n *\n * RAG - Extract Text: re-read every new/changed document from the inventory\n * and extract text elements through the rag_core extractor registry into the\n * promoted CAS table <project>_ELEMENTS (varchar - no 32k limit). A corrupt\n * document is marked failed in the inventory and never fails the flow.\n * Thin shell over rag_core.steps.run_extract - see the About tab.\n ******************************************************************************/\n%macro _rgex_setup;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_ragProject) %then %global _rgex_ragProject;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_tablesCaslib) %then %global _rgex_tablesCaslib;\n%mend _rgex_setup;\n%_rgex_setup;\n%macro _rgex_inherit;\n    %local dsid vproject vcaslib rc;\n    %if %symexist(_rgex_inventory) %then\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_inventory)) NE 0 %then %do;\n        %if %sysfunc(exist(&_rgex_inventory.)) %then %do;\n            %let dsid = %sysfunc(open(&_rgex_inventory., i));\n            %if &dsid. NE 0 %then %do;\n                %let vproject = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., rag_project));\n                %let vcaslib = %sysfunc(varnum(&dsid., tables_caslib));\n                %if %sysfunc(fetch(&dsid.)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n                    %if &vproject. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgex_ragProject = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vproject.));\n                    %if &vcaslib. GT 0 %then\n                        %let _rgex_tablesCaslib = %sysfunc(getvarc(&dsid., &vcaslib.));\n                %end;\n                %let rc = %sysfunc(close(&dsid.));\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_ragProject)) EQ 0 %then %do;\n        data _null_;\n            putLog \"ERROR: RAG - Extract Text: the inventory does not name a RAG \"\n                   \"project - wire the output of RAG - List Documents into \"\n                   \"this step (steps older than version 1.2 do not carry it)\";\n            abort 42;\n        run;\n    %end;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_tablesCaslib)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgex_tablesCaslib = casuser;\n%mend _rgex_inherit;\n%_rgex_inherit;\n%macro _rgex_port_default;\n    %if not %symexist(_rgex_invout) %then %global _rgex_invout;\n    %if %length(%superq(_rgex_invout)) EQ 0 %then\n        %let _rgex_invout = rgexout.&_rgex_ragProject._INV_EXTRACT;\n%mend _rgex_port_default;\n%_rgex_port_default;\n\n%let _rgex_viyaHost = %sysfunc(getoption(SERVICESBASEURL));\n%let _rgex_rc = 1;\n%let _rgex_error = The Python program did not run.;\n%let _rgex_summary = ;\n%let _rgex_nel = 0;\n%let _rgex_ninv = 0;\n\n/* One CAS session for the whole step: created here, reused by\n   SWAT inside proc python, promote+save done by proc casutil.\n   rgexout is where the step's OUTPUT TABLE lands by default -\n   the same caslib as the pipeline tables, so a flow leaves its\n   intermediate results next to each other. */\ncas rgexcas uuidmac=_rgex_casuuid;\n%let _rgex_cashost = %sysfunc(getoption(CASHOST));\n%let _rgex_casport = %sysfunc(getoption(CASPORT));\nlibname rgexout cas caslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\" sessref=rgexcas;\n\n%macro _rgex_export(portvar, file);\n    %if %symexist(&portvar.) %then %do;\n        %if %length(%superq(&&portvar.)) GT 0 %then %do;\n            %if %sysfunc(exist(&&&portvar..)) %then %do;\n                filename _rgex_io \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/&file.\";\n                proc json out=_rgex_io noSASTags;\n                    export &&&portvar..;\n                run; quit;\n                filename _rgex_io clear;\n            %end;\n        %end;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgex_export;\n%_rgex_export(_rgex_inventory, rgex_inventory_in.json);\n\nproc python restart;\nsubmit;\ndef main():\n    import json\n    import os\n    import sys\n    import tempfile\n    import time\n    import traceback\n\n    def sas_safe(text):\n        \"\"\"Strings crossing into SAS.logMessage/SAS.symput are embedded into\n        generated SAS statements - quotes and macro characters corrupt the\n        code stream (verified live). EVERY such string goes through here.\"\"\"\n        cleaned = str(text)\n        for ch in (\"'\", '\"', \"%\", \"&\", \";\"):\n            cleaned = cleaned.replace(ch, \" \")\n        return cleaned\n\n    def M(msg):\n        SAS.logMessage(\"RAGEXTRACT \" + sas_safe(msg))\n\n    try:\n        import requests\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the requests package - see \"\n                                   \"the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n    try:\n        import pandas as pd\n        import swat\n    except Exception:\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_error\", \"The Python environment of this compute \"\n                                   \"context lacks the swat/pandas packages \"\n                                   \"required for the CAS table transport - \"\n                                   \"see the RAG administration guide.\")\n        return\n\n    BASE = str(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_viyaHost\") or \"\").rstrip(\"/\")\n    TOKEN = os.environ.get(\"SAS_SERVICES_TOKEN\", \"\")\n    AUTH = {\"Authorization\": \"Bearer \" + TOKEN}\n    VERIFY = os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\") or os.environ.get(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\") or True\n    WORKPATH = SAS.workpath if SAS.workpath.endswith(os.sep) else SAS.workpath + os.sep\n\n    P = {name: str(SAS.symget(name) or \"\").strip() for name in [\n        \"_rgex_extractor\",\n        \"_rgex_ragProject\",\n        \"_rgex_tablesCaslib\",\n        \"_rgex_ragCorePath\",\n    ]}\n\n    def read_rows(filename, missing_message):\n        path = WORKPATH + filename\n        if not os.path.exists(path):\n            raise RuntimeError(missing_message)\n        with open(path, \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            data = json.load(fh)\n        rows = []\n        for row in data if isinstance(data, list) else []:\n            rows.append({str(k).lower(): v for k, v in row.items()})\n        return rows\n\n    def clean_path(raw):\n        \"\"\"Path-selector values arrive scheme-prefixed (sasserver:/...,\n        sascontent:/...); strip the scheme off.\"\"\"\n        value = str(raw or \"\").strip()\n        for scheme in (\"sascontent:\", \"sasserver:\"):\n            if value.lower().startswith(scheme):\n                return value[len(scheme):]\n        return value\n\n    STARTED = time.time()\n    SUMMARY = []\n\n    def summarize(line):\n        \"\"\"One line of the step's log summary (SAS prints them at the end).\"\"\"\n        SUMMARY.append(str(line))\n\n    def publish_summary(target):\n        elapsed = time.time() - STARTED\n        summarize(f\"elapsed {elapsed:.1f}s\")\n        SAS.symput(target, sas_safe(\" | \".join(SUMMARY))[:1500])\n\n    def write_rows(filename, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n        out = []\n        for row in rows:\n            rec = {}\n            for column in columns:\n                value = row.get(column)\n                if column in numeric:\n                    try:\n                        rec[column] = float(value or 0)\n                    except Exception:\n                        rec[column] = 0.0\n                else:\n                    rec[column] = \"\" if value is None else str(value)\n            out.append(rec)\n        with open(WORKPATH + filename, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            json.dump(out, fh)\n        return len(out)\n\n    try:\n        # ---- CAS: reuse the session the step created in SAS ---------------\n        # (sas-studio-custom-steps: Reuse-CAS-session-from-SWAT)\n        import re as _re\n        os.environ.setdefault(\"CAS_CLIENT_SSL_CA_LIST\",\n                              os.environ.get(\"SSLCALISTLOC\", \"\"))\n        conn = swat.CAS(hostname=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_cashost\") or \"\"),\n                        port=int(float(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_casport\") or 5570)),\n                        password=TOKEN,\n                        session=str(SAS.symget(\"_rgex_casuuid\") or \"\"))\n        CASLIB = P[\"_rgex_tablesCaslib\"] or \"casuser\"\n        if not _re.match(r\"^[A-Za-z][A-Za-z0-9_]{0,19}$\",\n                         P[\"_rgex_ragProject\"] or \"\"):\n            raise RuntimeError(\n                \"ragProject must be 1-20 characters (letters, digits, \"\n                \"underscores, starting with a letter) so every \"\n                \"project_suffix table name stays within the 32 characters \"\n                \"SAS Studio displays\")\n\n        def project_table(suffix):\n            return P[\"_rgex_ragProject\"] + suffix\n\n        def stamp(rows):\n            \"\"\"Every inventory row names its pipeline, so the next step\n            inherits the project and caslib instead of asking again.\"\"\"\n            for row in rows:\n                row[\"rag_project\"] = P[\"_rgex_ragProject\"]\n                row[\"tables_caslib\"] = CASLIB\n            return rows\n\n        def cas_read(name, required_message=None):\n            \"\"\"Read a pipeline table into lower-cased row dicts; absent\n            table = empty (the pipeline's empty state) unless required.\"\"\"\n            if not conn.table.tableExists(caslib=CASLIB, name=name).exists:\n                if required_message:\n                    raise RuntimeError(required_message)\n                return []\n            frame = conn.CASTable(name, caslib=CASLIB).to_frame()\n            rows = []\n            for record in frame.to_dict(\"records\"):\n                row = {}\n                for key, value in record.items():\n                    row[str(key).lower()] = None if pd.isna(value) else value\n                rows.append(row)\n            return rows\n\n        def label_columns(name, columns):\n            \"\"\"Put the shipped column labels on a CAS table - they survive\n            the promote, so the pipeline tables read without the schema.\"\"\"\n            try:\n                from rag_core.steps import column_labels\n                labels = column_labels(columns)\n                if labels:\n                    conn.table.alterTable(\n                        caslib=CASLIB, name=name,\n                        columns=[{\"name\": column, \"label\": label}\n                                 for column, label in labels.items()])\n            except Exception as exc:\n                M(f\"column labels not applied to {name}: {exc}\")\n\n        def cas_stage(name, rows, columns, numeric=()):\n            \"\"\"Upload the session-scope staging table <name>_S with varchar\n            columns (no 32k limit); the SAS side swaps it into the promoted\n            global table and saves it, so the previous state survives a\n            mid-step failure.\"\"\"\n            if not rows:\n                return 0\n            data = []\n            for row in rows:\n                rec = []\n                for column in columns:\n                    value = row.get(column)\n                    if column in numeric:\n                        try:\n                            rec.append(float(value or 0))\n                        except Exception:\n                            rec.append(0.0)\n                    else:\n                        rec.append(\"\" if value is None else str(value))\n                data.append(rec)\n            frame = pd.DataFrame(data, columns=list(columns))\n            spec = [{\"name\": column,\n                     \"type\": \"double\" if column in numeric else \"varchar\"}\n                    for column in columns]\n            conn.upload_frame(frame,\n                              casout={\"name\": name + \"_S\", \"caslib\": CASLIB,\n                                      \"replace\": True},\n                              importoptions={\"fileType\": \"csv\",\n                                             \"allowEmbeddedNewLines\": True,\n                                             \"vars\": spec})\n            label_columns(name + \"_S\", columns)\n            return len(rows)\n\n        # ---- rag_core bootstrap: download the governed SAS Content folder --\n        def get_json(endpoint, **params):\n            response = requests.get(BASE + endpoint, params=params, headers=AUTH,\n                                    verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n            response.raise_for_status()\n            return response.json()\n\n        def download_folder(folder_id, local_dir):\n            os.makedirs(local_dir, exist_ok=True)\n            count = 0\n            members = get_json(f\"/folders/folders/{folder_id}/members\", limit=200)\n            for member in members.get(\"items\", []):\n                uri = member.get(\"uri\", \"\")\n                if \"/files/files/\" in uri:\n                    content = requests.get(BASE + uri + \"/content\", headers=AUTH,\n                                           verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 60))\n                    content.raise_for_status()\n                    with open(os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]), \"wb\") as fh:\n                        fh.write(content.content)\n                    count += 1\n                elif \"/folders/folders/\" in uri:\n                    count += download_folder(uri.rsplit(\"/\", 1)[-1],\n                                             os.path.join(local_dir, member[\"name\"]))\n            return count\n\n        core_path = (clean_path(P[\"_rgex_ragCorePath\"])\n                     or \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\")\n        root = requests.get(BASE + \"/folders/folders/@item\",\n                            params={\"path\": core_path}, headers=AUTH,\n                            verify=VERIFY, timeout=(5, 30))\n        if root.status_code != 200:\n            raise RuntimeError(f\"rag_core folder {core_path} not found \"\n                               f\"(HTTP {root.status_code}) - deploy it per the \"\n                               \"administration guide\")\n        staging = tempfile.mkdtemp(prefix=\"rag_core_\")\n        n_files = download_folder(root.json()[\"id\"], os.path.join(staging, \"rag_core\"))\n        sys.path.insert(0, staging)\n        import rag_core\n        M(f\"rag_core {rag_core.RAG_CORE_VERSION} bootstrapped ({n_files} files)\")\n\n        from rag_core.extractors import ExtractorRegistry\n        from rag_core.sources import reader_for\n        from rag_core.steps import (ELEMENT_COLUMNS, INVENTORY_COLUMNS,\n                                    run_extract)\n\n        inventory_columns = INVENTORY_COLUMNS\n        inventory = read_rows(\"rgex_inventory_in.json\",\n                              \"the inventory input port is not connected - \"\n                              \"wire the RAG - List Documents output into \"\n                              \"this step\")\n        registry = ExtractorRegistry()\n        catalog = registry.catalog()\n        unavailable = catalog[\"unavailable\"]\n        if unavailable:\n            M(f\"extractors unavailable (packages missing): {unavailable}\")\n\n        # documents keep their source: the step re-reads them where the List\n        # step found them, so no second folder has to be picked here\n        kinds = sorted({(row.get(\"source_kind\") or \"path\") for row in inventory\n                        if row.get(\"status\") in (\"new\", \"changed\")})\n        source = None\n        for kind in kinds:\n            source = source or reader_for(kind, BASE, TOKEN, VERIFY)\n        forced = P[\"_rgex_extractor\"]\n        if forced in (\"\", \"auto\"):\n            forced = None\n\n        elements, updated = run_extract(inventory, registry,\n                                        extractor_name=forced,\n                                        source=source, log=M)\n        n_elements = cas_stage(project_table(\"_ELEMENTS\"), elements,\n                               ELEMENT_COLUMNS, numeric=(\"level\", \"page\"))\n        n_inventory = write_rows(\"rgex_inventory_out.json\", stamp(updated),\n                                 inventory_columns, numeric=(\"chunk_count\",))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_nel\", str(n_elements))\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_ninv\", str(n_inventory))\n        n_docs = sum(1 for r in updated\n                     if r.get(\"extractor\") and r.get(\"status\") != \"failed\")\n        n_failed = sum(1 for r in updated if r.get(\"status\") == \"failed\")\n        used = {}\n        for row in updated:\n            if row.get(\"extractor\") and row.get(\"status\") != \"failed\":\n                used[row[\"extractor\"]] = used.get(row[\"extractor\"], 0) + 1\n        summarize(\"extractor: \" + (forced or \"chosen per file format\"))\n        summarize(f\"sources read: {', '.join(kinds) or 'none pending'}\")\n        summarize(f\"{n_docs} documents extracted, {n_failed} failed, \"\n                  f\"{n_inventory - n_docs - n_failed} skipped as unchanged\")\n        if used:\n            summarize(\"extractors used: \"\n                      + \", \".join(f\"{k}={v}\" for k, v in sorted(used.items())))\n        if unavailable:\n            summarize(f\"unavailable extractors: {', '.join(sorted(unavailable))}\")\n        summarize(f\"{n_elements} elements written to \"\n                  f\"{CASLIB}.{project_table('_ELEMENTS')}\")\n        publish_summary(\"_rgex_summary\")\n\n        try:\n            conn.close(close_session=False)\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_rc\", \"0\")\n    except Exception as error:\n        error_text = f\"{type(error).__name__}: {error}\"\n        M(\"failed: \" + sas_safe(error_text))\n        print(traceback.format_exc())\n        SAS.symput(\"_rgex_error\", sas_safe(error_text)[:500])\n\n\nmain()\nendsubmit;\nrun; quit;\nproc python terminate;\nrun; quit;\n\n%macro _rgex_swap(suffix, count);\n    %if &_rgex_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %if &count. LT 0 %then %return;\n    proc casutil sessref=rgexcas incaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\"\n                 outcaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\";\n        droptable casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix.\" quiet;\n        %if &count. GT 0 %then %do;\n            promote casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix._S\"\n                    casout=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix.\";\n            save casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix.\"\n                 casout=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix.\" replace;\n        %end;\n        %else %do;\n            deletesource casdata=\"&_rgex_ragProject.&suffix..sashdat\" quiet;\n        %end;\n    quit;\n%mend _rgex_swap;\n%_rgex_swap(_ELEMENTS, &_rgex_nel.);\n\n%macro _rgex_emit_inventory;\n    %if &_rgex_rc. NE 0 %then %return;\n    %local lib table opts;\n    %let lib = %upcase(%scan(&_rgex_invout., 1, .));\n    %let table = %scan(&_rgex_invout., 2, .);\n    %if &lib. EQ %upcase(rgexout) %then %do;\n        proc casutil sessref=rgexcas\n                     incaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\"\n                     outcaslib=\"&_rgex_tablesCaslib.\";\n            droptable casdata=\"&table.\" quiet;\n        quit;\n        %let opts = (promote=yes);\n    %end;\n    %else %let opts = (compress=yes);\n    %if &_rgex_ninv. GT 0 %then %do;\n        filename rgexino \"%sysfunc(pathname(work))/rgex_inventory_out.json\";\n        libname rgexinj json fileref=rgexino;\n        data &_rgex_invout.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\";\n            set rgexinj.root(drop=ordinal_root);\n        run;\n        libname rgexinj clear;\n        filename rgexino clear;\n    %end;\n    %else %do;\n        data &_rgex_invout.&opts.;\n            length doc_id $ 40 source_uri $ 1024 source_kind $ 16\n                   content_hash $ 64 mtime $ 32 status $ 12 error_text $ 512\n                   pipeline_version $ 32 config_hash $ 32 chunk_count 8\n                   run_id $ 32 updated_at $ 24 extractor $ 64\n                   rag_project $ 20 tables_caslib $ 32;\n            label doc_id=\"Document ID\" source_uri=\"Source location\"\n                  source_kind=\"Source type\" content_hash=\"Content fingerprint\"\n                  mtime=\"Source last modified\" status=\"Ingestion status\"\n                  error_text=\"Failure reason\" pipeline_version=\"Pipeline version\"\n                  config_hash=\"Configuration fingerprint\" chunk_count=\"Chunks produced\"\n                  run_id=\"Ingestion run ID\" updated_at=\"Row updated (UTC)\"\n                  extractor=\"Text extractor used\" rag_project=\"RAG project\"\n                  tables_caslib=\"Pipeline tables caslib\";\n            call missing(of _all_);\n            stop;\n        run;\n    %end;\n%mend _rgex_emit_inventory;\n%_rgex_emit_inventory;\n\nlibname rgexout clear;\ncas rgexcas terminate;\n\ndata _null_;\n    length part $ 500;\n    if \"&_rgex_rc.\" ne \"0\" then do;\n        putLog \"ERROR: RAG - Extract Text failed: %superq(_rgex_error)\";\n        abort 42;\n    end;\n    putLog \"NOTE: ----- RAG - Extract Text -----\";\n    do i = 1 to countw(\"%superq(_rgex_summary)\", \"|\");\n        part = strip(scan(\"%superq(_rgex_summary)\", i, \"|\"));\n        if part ne \"\" then putLog \"NOTE:   \" part;\n    end;\nrun;"}, "type": "code", "ui": "{\n\t\"showPageContentOnly\": true,\n\t\"pages\": [\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageDefinition\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Definition\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_info\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Extracts text elements from every new or changed document in the inventory into the promoted CAS table <project>_ELEMENTS. Formats: plaintext, markdown, CSV/JSON, HTML and the PDF text layer (pypdfium2); markitdown formats when that package is installed. A corrupt document is marked failed and skipped - the flow keeps running.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_inventory\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"inputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Document inventory (from RAG - List Documents):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_extractor\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"dropdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Text extractor:\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"items\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"auto\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Automatic (by file extension)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"csv_json\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"csv_json (.csv, .json, .jsonl, .ndjson, .tsv)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"html\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"html (.htm, .html, .xhtml)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"markdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"markdown (.markdown, .md)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"markitdown\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"markitdown (.docx, .epub, .pptx, .rtf, .xlsx)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"pdf-text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"pdf-text (.pdf)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"value\": \"plaintext\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"plaintext (.log, .text, .txt)\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t],\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_sectionAdvanced\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Runtime\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"path\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"SAS Content folder holding rag_core (set by the deployment - not editable here):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"pathtype\": \"folder\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"enabled\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"$_rgex_ragCorePath\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"=\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"__set_by_deployment__\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"_rgex_invout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"outputtable\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Updated inventory output (wire this one forward):\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"required\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"placeholder\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t},\n\t\t{\n\t\t\t\"id\": \"pageAbout\",\n\t\t\t\"type\": \"page\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"About\",\n\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textAbout\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"RAG - Extract Text step\\n==========\\n\\nRe-reads the bytes of every new or changed document and runs the rag_core extractor registry. Elements land in <project>_ELEMENTS (promoted + saved); when no documents are pending the table is removed - an absent table is the pipeline's empty state. Documents whose extraction fails are marked failed in the updated inventory and retry on the next run.\\n\\nFlow wiring: chain the document INVENTORY through every step - RAG - List Documents \u2192 Extract Text \u2192 Chunk Documents \u2192 Embed Chunks \u2192 Load Vector Store. The bulk data travels beside the flow in promoted CAS tables named <project>_ELEMENTS, <project>_CHUNKS, <project>_EMBEDDED and <project>_LEDGER in the tables caslib (each saved to disk, so state survives server restarts; names stay within 32 characters so they display nicely in SAS Studio). Each step's output table lands in that same caslib as <project>_INV_LIST, _INV_EXTRACT, _INV_CHUNK, _INV_EMBED and <project>_LOAD_REPORT unless you point the output port somewhere else. Give every step the SAME project name and caslib.\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Pre-requisites\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": false,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textPrereqs\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"Tested on SAS Viya 2026 (Stable).\\n\\n* The rag_core runtime must be deployed to SAS Content (default: /SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core) with deploy-rag-content.ps1/.sh - keep that folder read-only for regular users.\\n* The compute context's Python needs the requests, swat and pandas packages (swat/pandas carry the pipeline tables to CAS - varchar columns, no 32k limit).\\n* CAS available; the runner needs write access to the tables caslib.\\n* pypdfium2 for the PDF text layer, markitdown for Office formats (each optional - matching extractors deactivate when a package is missing).\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"sectionChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"section\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"label\": \"Changelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"open\": true,\n\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\"children\": [\n\t\t\t\t\t\t{\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"id\": \"textChangelog\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"type\": \"text\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"text\": \"* Version: 1.2 (29JUL2026)\\n      - SAS Content document sources; output tables land in the tables caslib; labelled columns; numeric and list-of-values fields; run summary in the log\\n* Version: 1.1 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Pipeline tables move to promoted CAS tables via SWAT (varchar, no 32k limit); automatic embed checkpoint\\n* Version: 1.0 (28JUL2026)\\n      - Initial version\",\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\"visible\": \"\"\n\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t\t\t]\n\t\t\t\t}\n\t\t\t]\n\t\t}\n\t],\n\t\"syntaxversion\": \"1.3.0\",\n\t\"values\": {\n\t\t\"_rgex_ragCorePath\": \"/SAS Agentic AI Accelerator/RAG/rag_core\",\n\t\t\"_rgex_extractor\": {\n\t\t\t\"value\": \"auto\",\n\t\t\t\"label\": \"Automatic (by file extension)\"\n\t\t}\n\t}\n}"}